<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="010" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Schema preflight — verify owner-created columns present</title>
    <phase>1 Data spine</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until-001</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>MINIMAL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Read-only verification of Dataverse schema existence; no code authored; the value is the gate decision, not implementation.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical existence check against a fixed schema contract — lowest judgment; low effort.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>low</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>HUMAN GATE (W1). All Phase-1/Phase-2 data + session code (011, 012, 013, 020…) assumes these columns exist; verification must complete and pass before any consumer runs.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>dataverse, preflight</tags>
    <estimated-effort>0.5-1 hour</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Verify that every owner-created Dataverse column this project consumes actually exists in the target environment,
    with the expected type/target, BEFORE any data-spine or session-binding code task runs. This is a HUMAN GATE: if
    any column is missing, BLOCK the dependent tasks and produce a clear owner-action list — do NOT create the schema
    yourself (the owner owns schema per spec Prerequisites).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Familiar with Dataverse metadata inspection (Web API `EntityDefinitions` / MCP
    `describe`) and the project's exact owner-created schema contract from spec.md Prerequisites.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A recorded verification (in `projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/schema-preflight.md`) confirming
    presence + type/target of all six owner-created schema elements; if any is absent, the note lists the exact
    owner-action items and the dependent tasks are marked blocked.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per spec Prerequisites (HUMAN GATE) + PLAN Phase 1.0, all net-new Dataverse schema is created by the owner; this
      project consumes it. The pipeline requires an explicit preflight so code tasks (011 type, 012 regarding, 013 file
      hop, 020 session FK) can assume the columns exist. `sprk_description` and `sprk_project` are confirmed created;
      the remaining owner columns must be verified before Phase 1+2 code runs.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file role="new">projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/schema-preflight.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Green e2e baseline established (Phase 0 gate cleared).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = verification ONLY. Do NOT create, alter, or migrate any Dataverse column — the owner owns schema. A missing column is a BLOCK + notify, never a create-it action (see escalation).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = the exact spec Prerequisites contract: `sprk_analysis.sprk_worktype` (Choice: agreement-analysis / legal-research / patent-application), `sprk_analysis.sprk_regardingmatter` (Lookup → sprk_matter), `sprk_analysis.sprk_regardingproject` (Lookup → sprk_project), `sprk_analysis.sprk_regardingdocument` (Lookup → sprk_document), `sprk_analysis.sprk_description` (multiline text), `sprk_aichatsummary.sprk_analysis` (Lookup FK → sprk_analysis). Verify logical name AND type/target for each.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>dataverse schema verification</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/skills/dataverse-mcp-usage/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>docs/data-model/</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="metadata describe" location=".claude/skills/dataverse-mcp-usage/SKILL.md">
        Use the Dataverse MCP `describe` / Web API `EntityDefinitions` read path to confirm attribute existence + type/target without mutating schema.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare MINIMAL rigor + reason. Load the spec Prerequisites schema contract.</step>
    <step order="1">For each of the 6 elements, query Dataverse metadata and record: present Y/N, logical name match, type, and lookup target (where applicable).</step>
    <step order="2">Cross-check the `sprk_worktype` Choice option values (agreement-analysis / legal-research / patent-application) resolve to real option-set members.</step>
    <step order="3">Write the results to notes/schema-preflight.md. If ALL present → mark the gate PASS. If ANY missing/mismatched → mark BLOCKED and produce an owner-action list (table + logical name + expected type/target).</step>
    <step order="4">If blocked, set the dependent tasks (011, 012, 013, 020) to ⛔ blocked in TASK-INDEX.md and notify the owner (🔔 Human Input Required). If pass, update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 010 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="5">Document the outcome in `projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any required column is absent or its type/target does not match the spec contract, STOP — do NOT create or modify the schema (owner owns it). Emit 🔔 Human Input Required with the exact owner-action list and block dependent tasks per CLAUDE.md §6.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">Read Dataverse metadata (describe / EntityDefinitions) — read-only.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/schema-preflight.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the target environment, when the preflight runs, then all 6 owner-created elements are confirmed present with matching logical name + type/target, and the gate is recorded PASS in notes/schema-preflight.md.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`sprk_worktype` is a Choice column and its three option values (agreement-analysis, legal-research, patent-application) are confirmed present.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: if a column is absent or mismatched, the task blocks with a clear owner-action list (element, logical name, expected type/target) and dependent tasks 011/012/013/020 are marked ⛔ blocked — the schema is NOT created by this task.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no Dataverse schema mutation is performed (verify by confirming only read/describe calls were issued).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec Prerequisites (HUMAN GATE) + PLAN Phase 1.0. `sprk_description` (multiline) + `sprk_project` logical name already
    confirmed by owner 2026-07-28; `sprk_documentid` is KEPT as the SPE subject-pointer and is a separate role from
    `sprk_regardingdocument` (do not conflate).
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge files. Follow task-execute (MINIMAL rigor; Step 9.5 gates skipped).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
